# Client B of the players scenario: joins a little later and holds ArrowUp briefly.
# Join takes real time that a tick count cannot predict (a slow browser needs seconds): wait for it.
wait_until 3000 assert.net_joined
# A short hold: the players module accelerates faster than friction slows, so a long one (64 ticks)
# can slide a cube off the ground, depending on timing (see CLAUDE.md, players tuning).
input.key_down ArrowUp
wait 16
input.key_up ArrowUp
wait 488
net.bodies
net.stats
# Traffic budget (measured: about 3 KB sent, 13-23 KB received) with headroom. Corrections depend
# on real timing; the bound only catches a prediction that stopped converging.
assert.net_bytes_below sent 20000
assert.net_bytes_below received 100000
assert.net_corrections_at_most 200
quit
